BT /F1 16 Tf 54 750 Td (4.3 Organelles and their jobs) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 724 Td (cell membrane: a thin, flexible layer that controls what enters and leaves the cell.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 709 Td (cytoplasm: the gel-like material inside the cell where many chemical reactions happen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 694 Td (nucleus: holds the cell's DNA and directs the cell's activities.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 679 Td (mitochondria: release energy from food \(sugar\) in a process called cellular respiration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 664 Td (ribosomes: build proteins. They are found in every cell, prokaryotic and eukaryotic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 649 Td (endoplasmic reticulum: a folded network that moves materials around the cell.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 634 Td (Golgi apparatus: packages proteins and sends them where they are needed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 619 Td (vacuole: stores water, food and wastes. Plant cells usually have one large central vacuole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 604 Td (lysosomes: break down worn-out cell parts and wastes \(mostly in animal cells\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 589 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 16 Tf 54 574 Td (4.4 Plant cells and animal cells) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 548 Td (Plant cells have three structures most animal cells do not:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 533 Td (- a cell wall outside the membrane that gives support and shape,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 518 Td (- chloroplasts, where photosynthesis turns light energy into chemical energy stored in sugar,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 503 Td (- a large central vacuole that helps the plant stay firm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 488 Td (Both kinds of cells have a membrane, cytoplasm, a nucleus, mitochondria and ribosomes.) Tj ET
endstream
